    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start. but i'm worried about the pushback from the more traditionalist members of the board. they're gonna argue that we have a fiduciary duty to maximize returns for shareholders and that ESG is just a distraction or even a drain on profits. how should i frame the argument that their view is basically obsolete, and what are the specific ways their 'short-termism' is actually going to hurt our bottom line in the long run?",
