      "content": "To counter traditionalists, frame your ESG argument not as a deviation from fiduciary duty, but as its modern evolution: ignoring systemic environmental and social risks is fundamentally bad business, much like ignoring a impending supply chain collapse. The \"short-term profit\" you seek today is actually a longer-term liability, as companies adhering to outdated models face higher capital costs, regulatory fines, and talent fractures that will inevitably erode their valuation. By now, the corporate world has recognized that sustainable governance creates the stable, dividend-generating assets required to maximize shareholder value over time, whereas traditionalism blinds you to these future risks. Presenting ESG as a shield against future bankruptcy rather than a marketing trend will help these board members see their legacy views as obsolete liabilities.",
